---
import "@fontsource/inter/400.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/500.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/600.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/700.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

<title>William "Billy" Braasch</title>
<meta
name="description"
content="Personal website of William “Billy” Braasch, a postdoctoral researcher in quantum information science at QuICS, University of Maryland."
/>
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />

<style>
:root {
--background: #f5f6f8;
--foreground: #111827;
--muted: #4b5563;
--light-muted: #6b7280;
--rule: #d7dce3;
--accent: #334155;
--link: #1f4f7a;
}

* {
box-sizing: border-box;
}

html {
font-family:
"Inter",
system-ui,
-apple-system,
BlinkMacSystemFont,
"Segoe UI",
sans-serif;
background: var(--background);
color: var(--foreground);
scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

body {
margin: 0;
min-height: 100vh;
background: var(--background);
-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
-moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
}

main {
width: min(100%, 73rem);
margin: 0 auto;
padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem) clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
}

.profile {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: 8.2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
gap: 1.6rem;
align-items: start;
padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
}

.portrait {
width: 8.2rem;
height: 8.2rem;
border-radius: 999px;
object-fit: cover;
border: 3px solid white;
box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--rule);
background: white;
}

h1 {
margin: 0;
color: var(--foreground);
font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
font-weight: 700;
letter-spacing: -0.045em;
line-height: 1.05;
}

.affiliation {
margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
color: var(--muted);
font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.2rem);
line-height: 1.5;
}

.description {
max-width: 56rem;
margin: 1rem 0 0;
color: var(--muted);
font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.18rem);
line-height: 1.55;
}

.links {
display: flex;
flex-wrap: wrap;
gap: 0.7rem 1.2rem;
margin-top: 1.45rem;
padding: 0;
list-style: none;
}

.links a {
color: var(--muted);
font-size: 0.96rem;
font-weight: 600;
text-decoration: none;
}

.links a:hover {
color: var(--link);
text-decoration: underline;
text-underline-offset: 0.22em;
}

.content {
max-width: 68rem;
border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
padding-top: 2.25rem;
}

section {
max-width: 64rem;
margin-bottom: 2.35rem;
}

h2 {
margin: 0 0 1rem;
color: var(--foreground);
font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.3vw, 1.75rem);
font-weight: 700;
letter-spacing: -0.035em;
line-height: 1.2;
}

p {
max-width: 62rem;
margin: 0;
color: var(--foreground);
font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.4vw, 1.15rem);
line-height: 1.65;
}

p + p {
margin-top: 1rem;
}

a {
color: var(--link);
text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
text-underline-offset: 0.22em;
}

a:hover {
color: var(--foreground);
}

.site-footer {
margin-top: 3rem;
padding-top: 1rem;
border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
color: var(--light-muted);
font-size: 0.84rem;
line-height: 1.5;
}

.site-footer a {
color: inherit;
}

@media (max-width: 680px) {
main {
padding-top: 1.25rem;
}

.profile {
grid-template-columns: 1fr;
gap: 1rem;
}

.portrait {
width: 6.5rem;
height: 6.5rem;
}

.content {
padding-top: 1.75rem;
}
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<main>
<header class="profile">
<img
class="portrait"
src="/images/billy.jpg"
alt="Portrait of William Braasch"
/>

<div>
<h1>William "Billy" Braasch</h1>

<p class="affiliation">
Postdoctoral researcher at
QuICS, University of Maryland
</p>

<p class="description">
Quantum thermodynamics, quantum algorithms, and mathematical structures of nonclassicality
</p>

<ul class="links" aria-label="Selected links">
<li>
<a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=uLIvPloAAAAJ">
Google Scholar
</a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="mailto:wbraasch@umd.edu">Email</a>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</header>

<div class="content">
<section id="research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
<h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2>

<p>
I study the mathematical structures that distinguish quantum 
theory from classical theories, including noncommutativity, 
symmetry, contextuality, quasiprobability, and thermodynamic 
constraints. I use these structures to understand the capabilities 
and limitations of quantum information processing.
</p>

<p>
My recent work connects quantum thermodynamics, quantum algorithms, 
and mathematical physics, with projects on Hamiltonian simulation, 
noncommuting conserved quantities, and quasiprobability representations 
such as the Kirkwood–Dirac and Wigner distributions.
</p>

</section>

<section id="outside-research" aria-labelledby="outside-heading">
<h2 id="outside-heading">Hobbies</h2>

<p>
Outside research, I spend as much time as I can in the mountains
and forests of New England. I particularly enjoy rock climbing and
cross-country skiing. I also like eating yogurt with a mini spatula.
</p>
</section>

<section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
<h2 id="contact-heading">Contact</h2>

<p>
Feel free to reach me at
<a href="mailto:wbraasch@umd.edu">wbraasch@umd.edu</a>.
</p>
</section>
</div>

<footer class="site-footer">
Built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>.
</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
